div.p:
A considerable part of the country is low, hot, and inhabited by the negro race;
                    the remainder high, temperate or cold, and inhabited by Indians, whites, and
                        Mestizoes.

A pure negro is something lower in the social scale than any other class, except
                    the pure Indian. Politically there is no distinction, and not much practically;
                    only that the uneducated, laboring Indian is virtually a peon or a slave.
